WEBVTT

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.580
<i>Joe Gibson Jr, huh?</i>

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:10.290
<i>For now,</i>

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.590
<i>if this could be called my preliminary before facing Gibson,</i>

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:17.750
<i>I can't lose to his kid here!</i>

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.600
W-Wait a moment!

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.100
This is inconvenient, really inconvenient for me!

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.310
Double A- No, Single A is okay! Please don't fire me!

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:39.680
It's an order from the owner.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:42.280
It's a pity, but it's already been decided.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:49.170
Though, there are still some other teams that are holding special Minor League tryouts.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.860
It's in Tennessee though, but I've prepared a letter of introduction.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:55.330
Take this with you and visit them.

00:00:55.330 --> 00:01:00.200
I hope to see you shine on a new field. 

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:03.740
After our quarrel,

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.760
it seems you worked on breaking balls.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.890
What? You got a problem with that?

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.380
You're still young.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:16.310
Rather than imitating an old man,
concentrate on your fastball more!

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:21.480
If you can gain true control over your serious fastballs,

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.240
you'll be able to strike out even Bolton and Gibson Jr!

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:08.080
<i>It's huge. </i>

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.460
<i>America is too huge.</i>

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:15.800
<i>It takes three hours by plane from Phoenix to Memphis!</i>

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:24.030
<i>And, on top of that, I don't know what time it is because of the different time zones, even when I'm still in the same America.</i>

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.980
Attention all passengers. 

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:31.050
We are now arriving at Memphis International Airport.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:39.710
<i>Believe in yourself and do your best, boy!</i>

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:41.950
<i>If you add accuracy to your fastball, </i>

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:45.010
<i>the day when you rise to the Majors will definitely come! </i>

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:46.830
<i>Don't be impatient. </i>

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:51.500
<i>Make sure you get stronger playing in the Minors,
and then we'll meet again at the top. </i>

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:57.650
I'll do this!

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:06.880
Let's see... 

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:10.400
First, I'll go to the Memphis Bats' headquarters.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.030
I think Fox gave me a note that says where to board the bus.

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:27.460
I'm sorry! Are you all right?

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:31.360
No... I'm fine. I'm fine.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:34.650
Okay, okay, no problems!

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.780
Huh? Are you Japanese?

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:40.750
What? You are too?

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:43.330
Is this fate? {meeting her}

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:45.220
Well, I'll be!

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:59.740
This is dangerous! I was almost tricked again!

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:02.700
That trick won't work on me again!

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.210
T-Trick? What do you mean?

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:07.780
Where's your partner?

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:08.840
What are you doing?

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:10.200
Don't play dumb!

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.870
You damn luggage stealing crime gang!

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:13.520
While the woman distracts the victim, 

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:16.380
her partner walks away with their luggage; that's how you do it, right?

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:17.980
Walking away with someone's luggage?

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:21.050
Why in the world would I try to steal your small dirty luggage?

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:23.660
Shut up! I'll take you to the police!

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:25.980
It hurts! Let me go!

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:27.900
I won't let you go, you sneaky thief!

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:30.650
Huh?

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:33.730
I-I'm sorry!

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:35.820
Very sorry!

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.650
So he wasn't trying to kidnap you after all?

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:40.600
Well,

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:43.410
you could say he was trying to do something similar to that.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:48.120
Whatever the case is, please don't act on your own at the airport.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:50.480
If anything happened to you, Miss Alice, 

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:53.080
as your bodyguard, my head would be the one that rolled.

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:58.840
And I was the one who thought I could sneak away behind your back to lay down and relax.

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:01.110
Come on. Let's go. 

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:03.360
A car is waiting for you.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:04.820
Yes.

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:12.090
I was really scared.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:13.810
Who are those people?

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:14.480
Wha-!?

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:20.580
G-Gone!

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:21.740
G-Gone!

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:26.700
My luggage is gone again!

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:36.300
<i>This is bad...</i>

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:41.430
<i>They even took my letter of introduction for the tryouts that I got from the Cougars' boss.</i>

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:44.800
The money and card that I got are safe, but still...

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:47.440
I'll have to take the tryout empty-handed again.

00:06:57.270 --> 00:07:01.100
I'm telling you that if you call them and ask, you'll know!

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.690
Telephone the Cougars! 

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:04.490
I am Goro Shigeno!

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:07.290
Tryout please! Please!

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:08.860
I haven't heard anything.

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:12.020
I can't let someone in without an invitation.

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:14.210
Get out of here! 

00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:16.290
I'm begging you; let me in!

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:19.590
Do you want me to die by the roadside here!?

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:21.530
You're getting on my nerves!

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:23.320
I'll call the cops!

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:24.940
I'm telling you...

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.490
What's wrong?

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:28.180
Huh?

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:34.900
Miss Alice?

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:37.690
What? Why are you here?

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.290
Hey, you jerk!

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:41.070
Where's my bag!?

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.680
And where did your huge companion go!?

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.040
I'm sorry!

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:51.410
I see.

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:58.030
Who'd think that you, who called me a luggage thief at the airport, would be Shigeno Goro.

00:07:58.030 --> 00:07:58.960
H-How do you know my name?

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:01.000
H-How do you know my name?

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.730
Don't worry.

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:06.420
Miller-san, from the Salmons, told me about you.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:09.420
He said that you'd be coming to take our tryout.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:10.920
"Our," you say? 

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:14.230
You two really aren't luggage thieves?

00:08:14.230 --> 00:08:17.340
That's rude. Of course we aren't!

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:19.350
He's my bodyguard,

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:20.880
Kevin Gordon.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:23.240
B-Bodyguard?

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:25.780
I am Jinnai Alice. 

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:30.700
I'm acting as an agent, but for now I'm the owner of the Triple A Memphis Bats.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:33.730
O-Owner!?

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:35.120
O-Owner!?

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:37.090
Acting as an agent, though.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:39.800
You're saying your name is Jinnai Alice?

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:45.130
Why is a Japanese girl a substitute owner for a Minor League team?

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:49.050
I didn't say a word about me being of Japanese nationality.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:55.750
My father is of Japanese descent and lived in America, but my mother is American.

00:08:55.750 --> 00:09:01.400
My mother's father, in other words, my grandfather, manages the Triple A Bats.

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.260
Grandfather?

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:06.570
My grandfather's physical condition has become worse,

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:10.330
so I've been working as an agent since last year in his place as the owner.

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:14.250
Well anyway, welcome.

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:20.650
Even if I say owner, 

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:23.300
I'm just barely earning enough profit to support myself.

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:25.200
Just like for the players, 

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:29.820
the money and the circumstances are incomparable to the Majors.

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:33.530
But...

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:41.760
When it comes to passion for baseball, we're all the same.{AMS: do not fade this}

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:49.670
Strike out!

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:55.750
What are you doing, Garrett?

00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:59.910
When will you stop swinging at that high pitch?

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:01.650
I'm going out to the field now.

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:05.240
Answer me right now! When will it be? Tomorrow? The day after that?

00:10:05.240 --> 00:10:08.450
Try to think of yourself in my shoes, who keeps playing you!

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:10.870
Captain, the field, the field!

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:12.430
Mister Carter!

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:15.300
Alice!

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:17.230
I'm sorry to barge in here in the middle of a game.

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:18.640
Oh no, no worries. 

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:21.930
I've shown you an embarrassing scene again.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:26.240
Might he be the one the Salmons told us about?

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:27.390
Yes.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:29.250
This is Goro Shigeno. 

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:32.220
According to Mr. Miller his qualities are sufficient.

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:36.120
If it weren't for the owner's decision, they'd regret losing such a player.

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:40.050
If it's possible, could you let him take the test after the game is over?

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:43.800
No, I can't do that.

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:45.980
Huh? Why?

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:50.590
Hurry up, change into your uniform, and get to the bullpen, Shigeno!

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:54.680
It's an exhibition game.

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:56.450
There aren't any special regulations for it.

00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:58.980
Show me your abilities.

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.030
Safe!

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:10.700
What are you doing, you idiot? 

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:12.830
You should be able to get him out in that situation!

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:13.880
Shut up!

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:16.670
You should be thankful that I even caught it, you halfwit!

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:19.080
They're at it again.

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:18.400
What was that? 

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:20.080
What are you saying, you bastard?

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:23.810
Ball! Ball four!

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:25.290
Damn it!

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:34.260
Don't mind! Don't mind, Franco!

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:38.250
You!

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:40.150
It can't be helped if you get hit,

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:43.710
but you're too afraid to face the batter, you damn chicken.

00:11:43.710 --> 00:11:46.570
Hurry up, pack your things, and go back to your country!

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:49.910
Hey, boss!

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:51.620
We're changing pitchers!

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:55.960
That Sanders, he's deciding these things on his own again!

00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:59.950
Hey, have you gotten word if he's ready in the bullpen?

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:01.620
He says "okay"!

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:02.420
All right!

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:07.320
Attention please, pitching, number 56:

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:09.900
Goro Shigeno!

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:13.380
Goro... Shigeno?

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:15.850
Who is that?

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:20.130
Taking the mound in a game is a tough situation for a rookie to take a test in.

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:22.580
During this time, when the curtain rises before his very eyes,

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:25.610
if he's got the firepower to produce results, he'll pass.

00:12:25.610 --> 00:12:28.360
If he can't, he'll just fail.

00:12:28.360 --> 00:12:30.230
I see.

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:33.950
You're Japanese? Do you understand English?

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:36.820
<i>That's an amazing beard.</i>

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:39.660
Okay, I get it.

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:42.080
Then I'll just show you the signs.

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:43.720
This is fastball.

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:45.710
Second is slider.

00:12:45.710 --> 00:12:47.520
No thank you.

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:50.340
This is only!

00:12:50.340 --> 00:12:52.260
I love fastball!

00:12:57.640 --> 00:13:00.470
Now hitting, number 7: Muller!

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:04.440
<i>Oh my. </i>

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:08.860
<i>It doesn't seem like he's intending to strengthen our front.</i>

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:10.430
Play!

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:15.990
<i>When I came to America, to be honest, I was in a hurry.</i>

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:21.160
<i>I just thought about producing results and rising to the Majors,</i>

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:24.100
<i>so I lost myself.</i>

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:25.630
<i>Don't be in such a hurry!</i>

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:29.010
<i>Slowly, but surely, rise up to the Majors!</i>

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:32.770
<i>But I'm no longer lost!</i>

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:36.840
<i>I'm going to challenge this huge country with who I am!</i>

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:47.690
Strike!

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:58.970
This is a free fansub.

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:58.970
Not for sale or rent.

00:14:03.410 --> 00:14:04.500
Ball!

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:08.250
Ball!

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:09.650
Two balls!

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:10.710
One strike!

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:13.880
<i>This guy...</i>

00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:16.820
<i>His control is another matter, but...</i>

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:17.800
<i>he's fast!</i>

00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:23.010
<i>I can clearly see his attitude of fearlessly facing the opponent, unafraid of being hit.</i>

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:27.350
Out!

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:30.730
Okay!

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:32.280
Unbelievable!

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:35.370
Maybe I've found a real treasure!

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:39.360
He's good.

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:41.970
Now hitting, number 28: Nixson!

00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:47.990
<i>The fourth one, huh?</i>

00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:51.800
<i>Against people who've got power, pitching high is taboo.</i>

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:54.250
<i>I'll concentrate on aiming low...</i>

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:57.050
<i>and swing my arm!</i>

00:14:58.510 --> 00:15:00.420
Strike!

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.350
<i>Not bad. A good pitch!</i>

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:07.560
Even though he's only got one player out so far,

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:10.250
he somehow seems really impressive.

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:14.190
Even though he, a rookie, has to take a test in a situation like this without warning,

00:15:14.710 --> 00:15:16.860
he's not agitated at all.

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:20.990
Strike two! {Not sure, sounds more like struck though. But you can't say it like that anyway, I think?}

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:26.610
Yeah. He's indeed calm.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:30.600
These last years, we've always made the playoffs, but...

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:32.930
every year victory eludes us, leaving us in second place.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:36.910
Because of our Achilles' heel, the lack of a closer.

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:40.370
But... that might be solved now!

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:43.730
Strike out!

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:48.950
<i>All right!</i>

00:15:48.950 --> 00:15:50.060
<i>Just one more!</i>

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:51.790
Okay!

00:15:51.790 --> 00:15:54.740
It's true that he may be able to fit in as the closer, but...

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:57.870
the problem isn't that simple.

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:07.910
After all, the reason we haven't raised a good closer...

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:12.540
is because of everyone <i>except</i> the pitcher.

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:13.950
Okay!

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:15.790
I got it!

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:17.540
I got it!!

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:19.210
I got it!!!

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:22.780
No!

00:16:23.780 --> 00:16:25.100
Look, there it is.

00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:28.360
Where are you looking, you bastard!?

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:31.560
Shut up! You were the one who ran into me!

00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:33.530
What are you doing, you idiots!?

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:35.620
Back home!

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:44.310
Damn it!

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:46.860
It's both of your faults that the score was tied!

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:51.290
I won't forgive you guys if I don't make it in time for my date with Jenny!

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:53.290
Shut up, you halfwit!

00:16:54.220 --> 00:16:57.110
T-This can't be!

00:16:57.110 --> 00:17:01.050
It was supposed to be game over with the last player getting out...

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:04.840
Now hitting, number 12: Winston!

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:06.640
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:17:06.640 --> 00:17:09.390
<i>Their bad habit has surfaced again.</i>

00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:15.090
Wait a minute! If they can't field at this important time,
the closer will go to waste!

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:20.900
The goal of this camp was to improve the team's fielding abilities.

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:23.320
Their effectiveness hasn't improved at all!

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:25.100
It can't be helped. 

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:28.660
This is all a part of the Bats' color, after all.

00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:32.710
What a careless thing to say.

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:37.060
We'll be the worst team in the league at fielding and number of errors this year too!

00:17:39.670 --> 00:17:40.920
Okay!

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:42.420
<i>We got him! {Got the batter}</i>

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:49.630
A comeback...

00:17:57.140 --> 00:17:58.940
<i>You guys!</i>

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:00.900
<i>If you can't field, then I won't bother with you!</i>

00:18:02.410 --> 00:18:03.690
Strike out!

00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:10.780
Damn!

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:12.910
This is unbelievable!

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:15.280
Hey, Shigeno!

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:15.870
Huh?

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:18.920
You're not responsible for losing the game.

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:20.540
You pass the test!

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:23.690
Congratulations!

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:26.080
He said that you passed the test!

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:29.080
I didn't think you'd pitch so well.

00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:33.360
Your contract will tie you to the Indiana Hornets,

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:36.540
but do your best with the Bats and try to aim for the top!

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:37.980
Oh, is that so?

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:39.770
What is it?

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:43.710
Well, I'm thankful to you for evaluating me, but...

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:46.180
please let me think a little before deciding on the contract.

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:47.200
Huh?

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:52.070
This isn't the only tryout that the Salmons introduced me to.

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:56.660
Sorry, but I want to improve myself on a better team.

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:58.050
What did he say?

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:03.790
Now hitting, number 4: Roy!

00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:07.120
The other Triple A teams I saw, the Cougars...

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:08.620
and the Falcons,

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:10.670
weren't weak teams like this one.

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:15.280
I want to take my time and get experience...

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:19.430
at a place with a level as close as possible to the Majors.

00:19:24.020 --> 00:19:25.150
Safe!

00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:27.370
Huh? He's fast!

00:19:28.190 --> 00:19:30.720
Now hitting, number 2: Kelloge!

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:32.680
Weak team?

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:36.950
I can't ignore that, Shigeno-kun.

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:38.200
What?

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:43.960
Now hitting, number 1: Buter.

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:45.660
It's true that...

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:47.380
the Bats have problems fielding,

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:52.260
and without a good closer, victory always evades our grasp.

00:19:52.260 --> 00:19:56.020
But they're strong enough to make the playoffs every year.

00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:59.060
It's a top-class Triple A team.

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:10.490
Safe! Safe!

00:20:10.490 --> 00:20:11.810
He did it!

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:12.950
First, we tie it up!

00:20:14.240 --> 00:20:17.240
Now hitting, number 13: Danston!

00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:21.770
A-A hitting team?

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:23.540
A-A hitting team?

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:25.000
Exactly.

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:26.630
They're a clumsy...

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:29.710
and rough bunch, with bruises all over their legs, but...

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:47.100
my grandfather and I love this totally dramatic team!

00:20:48.030 --> 00:20:50.610
Testee! Come join in too!

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:14.800
Delicious!

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:21.510
Shigeno-kun...

00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:26.770
I thought that maybe he would stay with us, but...

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:32.060
But I guess it can't be helped!

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:35.370
U-Um, yes?

00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:36.710
It's Kevin.

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:40.740
A homeless person is waiting in the lobby to see you, Miss.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:46.630
Come on, who is it at this time?

00:21:46.630 --> 00:21:49.930
I don't have any homeless acquaintances!

00:21:56.890 --> 00:21:57.940
Yo!

00:21:58.590 --> 00:22:00.460
Shigeno-kun...

00:22:01.070 --> 00:22:02.700
What happened?

00:22:02.700 --> 00:22:06.230
Didn't you leave to take the tryout for the Panthers?

00:22:06.230 --> 00:22:07.860
Well...

00:22:07.860 --> 00:22:11.150
No motels were vacant.

00:22:11.150 --> 00:22:12.020
So...

00:22:12.980 --> 00:22:15.800
If it's okay, can I stay here tonight?

00:22:16.700 --> 00:22:20.210
Of course, not for free.

00:22:20.210 --> 00:22:21.370
If you're okay with having me,

00:22:21.370 --> 00:22:25.580
I'll lend my strength and work for the Bats' victory together with those eccentric fellows.

00:22:34.840 --> 00:22:37.600
Welcome to the Memphis Bats!

00:24:11.450 --> 00:24:13.850
While I'm running around in America,

00:24:13.850 --> 00:24:17.650
pro baseball camps have begun in Japan too.

00:24:17.650 --> 00:24:18.980
Toshiya!

00:24:18.980 --> 00:24:22.130
Show them your skills!

00:24:22.780 --> 00:24:24.180
Next time, on Major:

00:24:24.180 --> 00:24:25.530
Debut!

00:24:25.530 --> 00:24:28.190
Run to the stage of your dreams!
